---
import MathLayout from '../../../layouts/MathLayout.astro';
import { getPath } from '../../../utils/path';

const lang = 'en';
const currentPath = '/en/university/math-logic';
const title = 'Mathematical Logic';
---

<MathLayout {title} {lang} {currentPath}>
	<article>
		<h1>{title}</h1>
		<p class="intro">Mathematical logic corresponds to the Second Principle: mechanical deduction. When proving, you can temporarily ignore content and just follow the form.</p>

		<h2>The Core of Logic: Form Itself</h2>
		<div class="concept-card card">
			<p>The core of logic is form itself. Given a string of symbols, it transforms symbols according to rules without caring what the symbols represent. For example, Modus Ponens: from "if $P$ then $Q$" and "$P$", directly infer "$Q$".</p>
		</div>

		<h2>Spatial vs Temporal Nature</h2>
		<div class="two-columns">
			<div class="concept-card card">
				<h3>Spatial</h3>
				<p>Commutative law: $P \land Q \equiv Q \land P$ - two propositions side by side, order doesn't matter.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="concept-card card">
				<h3>Temporal</h3>
				<p>Transitivity of implication: $P \to Q, Q \to R \Rightarrow P \to R$ - clearly a chain of steps, a path from start to finish.</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<h2>Learning Path</h2>
		<div class="learning-path">
			<div class="path-step">
				<span class="step-num">1</span>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Propositional Logic</h3>
					<p>Propositions, connectives, truth tables, tautologies</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="path-step">
				<span class="step-num">2</span>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Predicate Logic</h3>
					<p>Quantifiers, predicates, variables, free and bound</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="path-step">
				<span class="step-num">3</span>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Proof Systems</h3>
					<p>Natural deduction, Hilbert systems, axiomatic systems</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="path-step">
				<span class="step-num">4</span>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Metalogic</h3>
					<p>Consistency, completeness, soundness, decidability</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="nav-footer">
			<a href={getPath('/en/university')} class="back-link">← Back to University Math</a>
		</div>
	</article>
</MathLayout>

<style>
	.intro {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.two-columns {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
		gap: 1rem;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.concept-card h3 {
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
		color: #f1f5f9;
	}

	.concept-card p {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}

	.learning-path {
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.path-step {
		display: flex;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding: 1rem 0;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.2);
	}

	.step-num {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		width: 2rem;
		height: 2rem;
		background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6366f1, #8b5cf6);
		border-radius: 50%;
		font-weight: bold;
	}

	.step-content h3 {
		margin: 0 0 0.25rem 0;
		color: #f1f5f9;
	}

	.step-content p {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}

	.nav-footer {
		margin-top: 3rem;
		padding-top: 2rem;
		border-top: 1px solid rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.2);
	}

	.back-link {
		color: #6366f1;
	}
</style>
